Theory Details ->
1) Upload and download functionality - When upload request is sent by client, metadata stored in the system and
signed url has been requested from S3, once we get signed URL from S3, its sent back to client and then client
directly upload to S3. Similarly during syc/download, url would be fetched from db and the file will be directly
fetched from S3.
2) Sync works - sync service fetches the metadata from db and see if anything has changes after given timestamp.
If yes it sends the metadata along with S3 links, so that client local will be in sync.
3) Client knows if the file has been already modified or it needs to be modify in local - with every file there
is a hashvalue value, if the hashvalue is changed it means that file is modified.
4) Changes in local folder identification and upload to S3 (if there is any change to local folder, it should
be synced) - there are some methods in windows/mac- which monitoe a location and if there is any change, it notifies.
5) how to upload big files from client to S3 - Client chunk the files according to bandwidth and size and these chunks
gets stored in the S3.
6) Quick sync - polling when the local folder is open
7) To utilize the bandwidth correctly, client cna compress the file and send it. mp4 files are already in compressed format
so only compress files whose compression will be beneficial
